Source: aurora-platform
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Aurora Silicon <noreply@aurorasilicon.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/aurora-platform
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: aurora-firstboot
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, cryptsetup-bin (>= 2:2.8), btrfs-progs, util-linux, coreutils, systemd, python3, passwd,
 sudo, kbd, procps, dracut, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Aurora per-install root encryption and Linux owner setup
 On an installed system's first boot, the initrd converts the root file system
 to LUKS2 in place with a temporary key; the desktop's own setup (or a text
 wizard) then creates the owner account, whose password replaces that key.

Package: aurora-power-budget
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, systemd, power-profiles-daemon, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CPU power budget for the power-saver profile on Apple Silicon
 Limits the CPU power budget while the power-saver profile is active, from
 values the machine reports.

Package: aurora-gamemode
Architecture: all
Depends: gamemode, ${misc:Depends}
Description: GameMode defaults for Apple Silicon
 Runs games on the performance cores and keeps the schedutil governor.

Package: aurora-secboot
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, systemd, systemd-ukify, sbsigntool, openssl, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Signed unified kernel images for the Aurora secure boot path
 Builds, and signs with the owner's key when one exists, a unified kernel image
 for each installed kernel. It does nothing until /etc/aurora/secboot.conf
 exists; see aurora-secboot(1).
